(Processes and Threads) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(A process is a program in execution with its own address space, registers and open) Tj T*
(files. A thread is the smallest unit of execution that the scheduler can run inside a) Tj T*
(process. Threads of the same process share memory and open files, which makes) Tj T*
(communication cheap but requires synchronization. A context switch saves the state of) Tj T*
(the running process and restores the state of the next one.) Tj T*
ET
