(Virtual Memory and Paging) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Virtual memory is a technique that gives each process the illusion of a large, private) Tj T*
(address space. Paging divides memory into fixed-size pages and frames, and the page) Tj T*
(table maps virtual pages to physical frames. A page fault occurs when a process accesses) Tj T*
(a page that is not in physical memory, so the operating system loads it from disk.) Tj T*
(Thrashing happens when the system spends more time handling page faults than running) Tj T*
(processes.) Tj T*
ET
endstream
