(Deadlocks) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(A deadlock is a state where a set of processes are each waiting for a resource held by) Tj T*
(another process in the set. Four conditions must hold for deadlock: mutual exclusion,) Tj T*
(hold and wait, no preemption and circular wait. Deadlock prevention breaks at least one) Tj T*
(of these conditions, for example by ordering resource requests. The banker's algorithm) Tj T*
(avoids deadlock by only granting requests that keep the system in a safe state.) Tj T*
ET
